brief_extract:
HARVEY, Joint Hon. Secretary, Newcastle (Staffs.) Branch, who is putting the money towards a food mixer. The main points in her re-planned kitchen were:
(1) back door moved;
(2) partitions forming larder, scullery and store removed;
(3) sink moved to another wall, and windows blocked up over old sink and former larder ; new double sink with cupboards under;
(4) copper removed and space for washing machine provided in working area;
(5) two-in-one heater under draining board;
(6) drying cabinet and broom cupboard in part of old storage space;
(7) cooker, and table top refrigerator;
(8) fluorescent light in working area with localised bracket lights; centre filament lamp and filament lamp over dining table;
(9) convector heater in dining recess and heater point in working area;
(10) 5 socket outlets in working area;
(11) ventilators over cooker and drying cabinet.
